AssetCollectionManifestV1.description:
Framework-owned zero-to-many media relation. The generated child table is
still an ordinary SQLite table for OCC, backup, and live-query purposes;
this descriptor is the exclusive authority to mutate it.
@ref LLP 0239#d2-assetcollection-is-the-zero-to-many-application-relation

permissionBacking.description:
Durable row-existence projection that grants the room permission in
sessions mode. The subject field equals the connection-bound user id;
every mapped table field equals its named room-scope field.

oneOf.description:
`v.vector(dimensions)` — an exact fixed-dimension binary64 vector.
Ordinary arrays keep their separate 1,024-item contract ceiling.

@ref LLP 0132#the-vvectordimensions-value

MediaFieldDescriptorV1.description:
Semantic facts for the finalized-only member of the AssetRef family.
The application column still contains only the opaque asset id.
@ref LLP 0244#d1-one-authoritative-media-result-materialization-cut

liveLimits.description:
Optional lower ceilings for the separately capability-gated live
search surface. Absence selects the target's admitted defaults.

@ref LLP 0136#capability-id-and-claim-discipline-llp-0119-oq2-proposal

VectorIndexManifestV1.description:
The complete table-local identity of one exact vector index.

@ref LLP 0132#vector-values-and-declarations — one version binds the vector
  field, dimensions, metric, release policy, ordering, and every work bound.
